# Nothing here is generated yet, but the rule is set now: a machine-written file is
# regenerated wholesale and never hand-edited, so a build or state directory would be
# a second source of truth the moment it appeared.

node_modules/
.dev/
.DS_Store
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# AGENTS.md is in ~/.gitignore_global, which is right for most repos and wrong for this one: here it is
# part of the deliverable, because the spec's §7 leans on it to make "knows nothing" safe. Re-included
# explicitly rather than force-added, so the exception is visible in the tree rather than remembered.
#
# Found the way the other two were: `git add` reported nothing and committed nothing. That is the third
# file today that was invisible to git while every status looked clean -- the spec (swallowed by
# /.config/* in workbench-env), its review, and this. Ask check-ignore, not status.
!AGENTS.md

# nix build output symlinks
result
result-*
